e Rhodopes.","cp":"nicaean-empire","cpn":"Empire of Nicaea","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Bulgarian_Empire","c":3},{"y":1255,"t":"gain","x":"1255: Macedonia regained.","cp":"nicaean-empire","cpn":"Empire of Nicaea","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Bulgarian_Empire","c":3},{"y":1256,"t":"loss","x":"1256: Nicaea takes it all back.","cp":"nicaean-empire","cpn":"Empire of Nicaea","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Bulgarian_Empire","c":3},{"y":1256,"t":"contest_end","x":"1256: the Nicaean contest ends with the loss of all the gains of 1254-1255.","cp":"nicaean-empire","cpn":"Empire of Nicaea","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Bulgarian_Empire","c":3},{"y":1260,"t":"gain","x":"1260: Vidin recovered.","cp":"kingdom-of-hungary","cpn":"Kingdom of Hungary","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Bulgarian_Empire","c":2},{"y":1261,"t":"loss","x":"1261: Vidin lost again.","cp":"vidin-1261","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Bulgarian_Empire","c":2},{"y":1263,"t":"loss","x":"1263: the Byzantines take the coast.","cp":"byzantine-empire","cpn":"Byzantine Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Bulgarian_Empire","c":3},{"y":1280,"t":"vassal_end","x":"c. 1280: the tribute to the Mongol Empire gives way to the Horde's overlordship (next event). No page dates the end; the year follows the ulus-of-jochi dossier's vassal_start. The Second Bulgarian Empire page: 'By the end of 1280' Ivaylo sought refuge with the Mongols.","cp":"mongol-empire","cpn":"Mongol Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Bulgarian_Empire","c":1},{"y":1280,"t":"vassal_start","x":"c. 1280: Bulgaria a vassal of the Horde. Second Bulgarian Empire page: George I Terter reigned twelve years 'bringing even stronger Mongol influence'; the page does not mention Nogai or a vassalage. Mirror of ulus-of-jochi /ledger/12 (confidence 1).","cp":"ulus-of-jochi","cpn":"Ulus of Jochi","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Bulgarian_Empire","c":1},{"y":1293,"t":"