g/wiki/Second_Bulgarian_Empire","c":2},{"y":1323,"t":"gain","x":"1323: Vidin and Tarnovo are one realm again.","cp":"vidin-1261","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Bulgarian_Empire","c":2},{"y":1331,"t":"gain","x":"1331: Ivan Alexander reconquers northeastern Thrace.","cp":"byzantine-empire","cpn":"Byzantine Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ivan_Alexander_of_Bulgaria","c":2},{"y":1332,"t":"gain","x":"1332: Rusokastro.","cp":"byzantine-empire","cpn":"Byzantine Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Velbazhd","c":2},{"y":1344,"t":"gain","x":"1344: Philippopolis and nine fortresses.","cp":"byzantine-empire","cpn":"Byzantine Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ivan_Alexander_of_Bulgaria","c":3},{"y":1356,"t":"split","x":"1356: Vidin breaks away.","cp":"despotate-of-vidin","cpn":"Tsardom of Vidin","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ivan_Shishman_of_Bulgaria","c":2},{"y":1356,"t":"split","x":"1356: Dobruja becomes a separate despotate.","cp":"despotate-of-dobruja","cpn":"Despotate of Dobruja","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Despotate_of_Dobruja","c":2},{"y":1366,"t":"loss","x":"1366: Varna, Emona and Kozyak to Dobrotitsa.","cp":"despotate-of-dobruja","cpn":"Despotate of Dobruja","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Despotate_of_Dobruja","c":3},{"y":1366,"t":"loss","x":"1366: the Savoyard crusade takes the Black Sea cities.","cp":"Savoyard crusade (Amadeus VI of Savoy)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ivan_Alexander_of_Bulgaria","c":3},{"y":1371,"t":"loss","x":"26 September 1371: Chernomen.","cp":"ottoman-empire","cpn":"Ottoman Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Bulgarian_Empire","c":3},{"y":1373,"t":"gain","x":"1373: Ihtiman and Samokov regained.","cp":"ottoman-empire","cpn":"Ottoman Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ivan_Shishman_of_Bulgaria","c":2},{"y":1373,"t":"vassal_start","x":"1373: Ivan Shishman becomes an Ottoman vassal.","cp":"ottoman-empire","cpn":"Ottoman Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ivan_Shishman_of_Bulgaria","c":2},{"y":1385,"t":"loss","x":"1385: Sofia falls.","cp":"ottoman-empire","cpn":"Ottoman Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ivan_Shishman_of_Bulgaria","c":2},{"y":1388,"t":"loss","x":"1388: the Ottomans take eastern towns.","cp":"ottoman-empire","cpn":"Ottoman Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ivan_Shishman_of_Bulgaria","c":2},{"y":1393,"t":"loss","x":"17 July 1393: Tarnovo falls.","m":7,"cp":"ottoman-empire","cpn":"Ottoman Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ivan_Shishman_of_Bulgaria","c":3},{"y":1393,"t":"capital_move","x":"1393: the seat moves to Nikopol (infobox 'Nikopol (1393-1395)').","m":7,"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Bulgarian_Empire","c":3},{"y":1393,"t":"vassal_end","x":"1393: the vassalage ends with the fall of Tarnovo (July 1393).","m":7,"cp":"ottoman-empire","cpn":"Ottoman Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ivan_Shishman_of_Bulgaria","c":2},{"y":1395,"t":"dissolve","x":"3 June 1395: Nikopol falls and Ivan Shishman is executed.","m":6,"cp":"ottoman-empire","cpn":"Ottoman Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ivan_Shishman_of_Bulgaria","c":3}],"wars":[{"name":"Uprising of Peter and Asen","from":1185,"to":1187,"outcome":"Isaac II beat the brothers in early 1186; they returned from over the Danube in the autumn with Cumans; the armistice 'de facto recognized Bulgarian independence' (1186 or early 1187).","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Bulgarian_Empire"},{"name":"Wars of Peter and Asen I with Byzantium (Third Crusade, Tryavna, Arcadiopolis, Serres)","from":1189,"to":1196,"outcome":"Asen and Peter occupied 'new territories of the Byzantine Empire' from July 1189; Isaac II beat the Cumans near Adrianople in April 1191; the Byzantines were beaten 'near Serres' in 1196, the year Asen was killed.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ivan_Asen_I_of_Bulgaria"},{"name":"Kaloyan's wars with Byzantium, Hungary and Serbia","from":1199,"to":1203,"outcome":"Braničevo, Velbuzhd, Skopje and Prizren in 1199 ('most probably'), Varna in 1201, Niš in the summer of 1203.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kaloyan_of_Bulgaria"},{"name":"Bulgarian-Latin war (Adrianople, Rusion, Philippopolis)","from":1205,"to":1208,"outcome":"Kaloyan's victory at Adrianople on 14 April 1205 and at Rusion in 1206 won most of Thrace; the Latins beat Boril at Philippopolis in 1208, 'reversing most of Kaloyan's gains'.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Bulgarian_Empire"},{"name":"Klokotnitsa campaign against Epirus","from":1230,"to":1230,"outcome":"Theodore Komnenos of Epirus was captured in March or April 1230; Macedonia, Thrace and 'Great Vlachia' in Thessaly passed to Bulgaria; Thessalonica became a vassal.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ivan_Asen_II_of_Bulgaria"},{"name":"Siege of Constantinople (1235-1236)","from":1235,"to":1236,"outcome":"Allied with Nicaea against the Latin Empire from 1235, the Bulgarians 'conquered the territories to the west of the Maritsa' (undated); John of Brienne and the Venetian fleet forced them to lift the siege before the end of 1235 and a second siege failed early…","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ivan_Asen_II_of_Bulgaria"},{"name":"Mongol invasion of Bulgaria (1242)","from":1242,"to":1242,"outcome":"'The Mongols invaded Bulgaria in 1242 and forced Bulgarians to pay a yearly tribute to them.'","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ivan_Asen_II_of_Bulgaria"},{"name":"Nicaean-Bulgarian wars (1246, 1254-1256)","from":1246,"to":1256,"outcome":"1246: Nicaea takes Adrianople, Serres, Skopje and Ohrid; 1254 Bulgaria regains the Rhodopes, 1255 Macedonia; 'All gains were lost in 1256.'","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Bulgarian_Empire"},{"name":"Hungarian-Bulgarian wars over Belgrade, Braničevo and Vidin","from":1211,"to":1261,"outcome":"1211 Boril cedes Belgrade and Braničevo; 1221 they return as Maria's dowry; Béla IV takes them in late 1231 or 1232; Hungary occupies them again after 1241; Vidin is recovered in 1260 and lost in 1261.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Bulgarian_Empire"},{"name":"Bulgarian-Byzantine war of Theodore Svetoslav","from":1304,"to":1307,"outcome":"Mesembria, Anchialos, Sozopolis, Agathopolis and the fortresses of northeastern Thrace in 1304; the peace of 1307 'acknowledging Bulgarian gains'.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodore_Svetoslav_of_Bulgaria"},{"name":"Battle of Velbazhd and the Bulgarian-Serbian war of 1330","from":1330,"to":1330,"outcome":"Serbian victory on 28 July 1330; 'The Bulgarians did not lose territory'; Michael Asen III was killed; Serbia advanced into Macedonia.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Velbazhd"},{"name":"Byzantine-Bulgarian war of 1331-1332 (Rusokastro)","from":1331,"to":1332,"outcome":"Ivan Alexander reconquered northeastern Thrace in 1331 and beat Andronikos III at Rusokastro in 1332, regaining 'many territories in Thrace'.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Velbazhd"},{"name":"Byzantine civil war (1341-1347), Bulgarian intervention","from":1344,"to":1344,"outcome":"The regency 'ceded him the city of Philippopolis' and nine fortresses in the Rhodopes in 1344.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ivan_Alexander_of_Bulgaria"},{"name":"Savoyard crusade (1366)","from":1366,"to":1366,"outcome":"Amadeus VI took Anchialus, Sozopolis, Messembria and Emona after Ivan Alexander refused John V safe conduct; Dobrotitsa, whose help was rewarded with Varna, Emona and Kozyak, fought on the other side.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ivan_Alexander_of_Bulgaria"},{"name":"Bulgarian-Ottoman wars","from":1371,"to":1395,"outcome":"Chernomen on 26 September 1371; vassalage in 1373; Sofia in 1382 or 1385; eastern towns in 1388; Tarnovo on 17 July 1393; Nikopol and Ivan Shishman's death in 1395.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ivan_Shishman_of_Bulgaria"}],"certainty":[{"from":1185,"to":1395,"level":"soft","note":"Frontiers are approximate throughout: the Danube is the only fixed line in the north; the Balkan and Rhodope mountains, the Struma and the Maritsa mark the south."}],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Bulgarian_Empire","title":"Second Bulgarian Empire"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kaloyan_of_Bulgaria","title":"Kaloyan of Bulgaria"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ivan_Asen_II_of_Bulgaria","title":"Ivan Asen II of Bulgaria"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ivan_Asen_I_of_Bulgaria","title":"Ivan Asen I of Bulgaria"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ivan_Alexander_of_Bulgaria","title":"Ivan Alexander of Bulgaria"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Velbazhd","title":"Battle of Velbazhd"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ivan_Shishman_of_Bulgaria","title":"Ivan Shishman of Bulgaria"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodore_Svetoslav_of_Bulgaria","title":"Theodore Svetoslav of Bulgaria"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Despotate_of_Dobruja","title":"Despotate of Dobruja"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_II_Komnenos_Doukas","title":"Michael II Komnenos Doukas"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skopje","title":"Skopje"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ni%C5%A1","title":"Niš"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stefan_Vladislav","title":"Stefan Vladislav"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boril_of_Bulgaria","title":"Boril of Bulgaria"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Budjak","title":"Budjak"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Bulgarian_monarchs","title":"List of Bulgarian monarchs"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Empire_of_Thessalonica","title":"Empire of Thessalonica"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Savoyard_crusade","title":"Savoyard crusade"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prizren","title":"Prizren"}]}